yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>75\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 72\u00b0F, and the record is 87\u00b0F (1902). The low of <strong>50\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Beaumont-Port Arthur has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Beaumont-Port Arthur's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Beaumont-Port Arthur has set <strong class=\"sig\">37 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 82 that chance alone would give, and <strong>111 record highs</strong>, more than the 81 that chance alone would give. The 1900s hold the most record highs of any decade (86). Beaumont-Port Arthur's all-time high is 111\u00b0F, on August 27, 2023.","t_chg":"Beaumont-Port Arthur's days and nights have warmed since 1986","p_chg":"Across 111 complete years: Beaumont-Port Arthur's average low shows no clear change: +0.03\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.05 to +0.11) that includes zero. Beaumont-Port Arthur's average high shows no clear change: +0.03\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.06 to +0.12) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.56\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.29 to +0.82) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.71\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.42 to +1.00). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in none; June fell.","t_rain":"Beaumont-Port Arthur has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Beaumont-Port Arthur's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+1.33 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.62 to +2.03), about +16.0 inches since 1904. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 62.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 2017 (104.30 in); the driest, 1917 (28.90 in). Beaumont-Port Arthur almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.4 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}